## Hooks

A `PostToolUse` hook on `Edit|Write|MultiEdit` runs `.claude/hooks/post-edit-reminders.sh`, which injects a short reminder into context after edits to sensitive files — project patterns from `naturalize.hook_patterns`, plus each stack pack's `post-edit-reminders.<pack>.sh` defaults (e.g. schema or IaC edits). Two `SessionStart` re-ground hooks keep a reset session on the rails: matcher `compact` → `.claude/hooks/post-compact-reground.sh` (after any context compaction); matcher `clear|resume` → `.claude/hooks/post-clear-reground.sh` (after a `/clear` or a `--continue`/`--resume`, which reload CLAUDE.md and the memory index but drop any loaded skill and the memory-file bodies — the hook re-injects the § Subagent orchestration discipline and nudges role sessions to re-invoke their skill). Run `/fleet-prime` to re-ground on demand. All are wired in [`.claude/settings.json`](.claude/settings.json).

## Subagent orchestration

How to dispatch and track subagents. This discipline lives in scattered memory files whose bodies only load on recall — so the essentials are pinned here (always loaded, survives `/clear`). The `subagent-liveness` skill is the detailed substrate.

- **Dispatch style decides whether the result comes back.** An **async background agent** (no `name`) returns its result to you automatically via a task-notification — use it when you just want an answer. A **named teammate** (`name:` set) is addressable but goes **idle holding its result**; you must message it to pull it. Don't route a "give me findings" job through a named teammate and then wait for a report that never pushes.
- **Never fire-and-forget.** After spawning any background/async agent, wait for its completion notification (or track it) before you report or move on. Never narrate, assume, or predict a pending agent's result — the completion notification is the only source of its output.
- **Long runners (> a few minutes)** — implementation, investigation, reviews, builds: use the `subagent-liveness` skill (register at spawn, watch for overdue/stale, probe before declaring death).
- **Short, single-concern agents; verify state live.** Prefer several focused agents over one god-agent, and read PR / issue / CI / merge state from GitHub, not from memory — a merge can leave a PR OPEN; confirm it actually merged before "done".
- **If a merge orchestrator owns the merge baton:** you don't merge. Finish the PR (local review clean + pre-push gate green, threads resolved), leave it a draft, and hand off per your merge-orchestration protocol.

## Context compaction

Context is cache; files and this repo are truth. Standing rules for every session, and doubly for long-runners (the monsters, fleet roles):

- Write what you'd miss the moment you learn it — per-PR quirks onto the PR, decisions into the relevant journal/state file, durable lessons into the lessons dir. Never save flushing for session end.
- After a compaction (a summary at the top of your context, plus the re-ground hook's note): re-read your skill's SKILL.md + config + state files and reconcile against live GitHub before acting. Treat summarized precision (PR numbers, SHAs, counters) as unverified.
- Long-running orchestrators prefer **rotation over marathon compaction**: at high context pressure with nothing in flight, post a digest, final heartbeat **"rotation requested"** (exact phrase), and stop — the fleet supervisor (agent-sessions skill) relaunches within minutes; restart recovers from durable state. Operator only on relaunch failure or a stale-but-alive session.

